body:
When using `OnActivity` the `turnState` is available in the configured handler.

I was expecting the values added in one turn to be available in future turns, however seems those are not persisted when Storage has not been configured

```cs
var agent = new AgentApplication(new AgentApplicationOptions() { StartTypingTimer = true })
    .OnActivity(ActivityTypes.Message, async (turnContext, turnState, cancellationToken) =>
    {
        int counter = turnState.GetValue("counter", () => 0);
        turnState.SetValue("counter", counter++);
        await turnContext.SendActivityAsync(MessageFactory.Text($"Echo [{counter}]: {turnContext.Activity.Text}"), cancellationToken);
    });
```

To avoid this issue we should consider some of these suggestions:

1. If Storage is required (memory storage as a minimum), make this requirement explicit in the AgentApplicationOption ctor (without having to use DI)
2. If storage is not provided, add memory automatically and produce a Warning

